<Project>
  <!--
    Temporary: silence NuGet audit warnings (NU1902, NU1903, NU1904) that are
    currently being treated as errors due to TreatWarningsAsErrors=true in
    build/Build.csproj.

    Why this exists
    The project pins log4net 2.0.15, which has GHSA-4f7c-pmjv-c25w
    (moderate severity). All GitHub releases have been failing since
    2026-05-16 (build-27) for this reason. The animation-pass release
    pipeline inherits the same failure.

    This file unblocks the release pipeline WITHOUT hiding the warnings
    from the build log. WarningsNotAsErrors only stops the "warning as
    error" promotion. The audit still runs and still emits the warning,
    so it remains visible for the actual remediation (bumping log4net
    to a non-vulnerable version).

    Remediation (TODO before this file can be deleted)
    1. Bump log4net 2.0.15 to a non-vulnerable version. The 2.0.x line
       appears abandoned; the latest is 3.3.2 as of 2026-07. log4net 3.x
       is a major-version jump with API changes (assembly loading,
       XmlConfigurator semantics) that needs a focused PR with QA.
    2. Audit other pinned packages for similar vulnerabilities.
    3. Delete this file once dotnet restore produces no NU1902/1903/1904.

    Until then, do not remove this file or the release pipeline will
    start failing again.
  -->
  <PropertyGroup>
    <WarningsNotAsErrors>NU1902;NU1903;NU1904</WarningsNotAsErrors>
  </PropertyGroup>
</Project>
